 this point  in time the warriors assumed that the  royal family had the founding titan  which is why she was going out of her  way to do this  after her close encounter with kenny  ackerman she again argued that they  should return to mali  but was overruled by reiner in this very  important scene this scene is a lot more  crucial than i think a lot of people  realize  but in order to explain it we need to  remember one thing  even after aaron was revealed to be a  shifter none of the warriors thought he  had the founding titan  in fact this was only confirmed at the  end of season 2. as far as they knew  the founding titan was still in  possession of the royal family and aaron  simply had the missing attack titan that  marley failed to capture  so the question then becomes if they  didn't think he had the founder  why did annie go out of her way to  capture him instead of trying to  complete the actual mission  in my opinion all goes back to this  conversation as she is clearly ready to  return to mali after five long years on  the island  despite that reiner insisted would be  pointless to go back with nothing to  show for it  rather than trying to retake the founder  annie had basically given up on the main  plan  and was trying to get aaron instead so  she could fulfill what rhino was saying  here  by acquiring the missing attack titan it  was at least something they could use to  maybe claim  that the mission was not a complete  failure if they had caught eren  annie would have been able to return  home to her father and possibly live out  the remaining year she has left  that's why she was crying after her  defeat because she knew she wouldn't be  able to fulfill the promise to return  next up we'll be looking at the ancient  female titans from the past  but bear in mind there will be major  spoilers ahead so if you're an anime  only and you haven't paused already  then now is definitely the time to do so  the first ancient titan we should talk  about is the 